/.idea/

# Locally generated operator files — never commit them to this public repo.
#
# `engine/scripts/provision-claude-md.sh` (the documented install step) reads
# `engine/identity.config` — which an adopter creates by copying the committed
# `engine/identity.config.example` — and renders `engine/CLAUDE.md.template`
# into a real `engine/CLAUDE.md`. Both files then hold that operator's own
# company name, personal name, timezone and private notes. Regenerating them
# is one command, so there is nothing to lose by keeping them out of version
# control, and everything to lose by committing them here.
#
# This rule lives at the repository ROOT and deliberately NOT in
# `engine/.gitignore`: `engine/UPGRADING.md` treats a filled-in `CLAUDE.md` as
# an adopter-owned file that an adopter may well want committed in their own
# repo, so the rule must not travel with a vendored copy of `engine/`. That is
# the same reasoning the rule carried before this repo stood on its own; only
# the root it is anchored to has changed.
/engine/identity.config
/engine/CLAUDE.md
/engine/CLAUDE.md.new

# Private source material, and anything derived from it.
#
# This repository gets published (see `.publication-boundary`). Recordings —
# and TRANSCRIPTS, MEASUREMENTS and TOOL OUTPUT built on them — belong here,
# where git will never carry them out.
#
# It was already the convention on 2026-08-29: the webinar audio sat at
# docs/reference/local/ and was correctly kept out. It was never written down,
# so the derived TEXT went in anyway, three lands running. Now it is a rule the
# machine reads: `.publication-boundary` names this path as a PRIVATE_SOURCES
# tree, and the publication guards both refuse a tracked write that reproduces
# anything found under it.
/docs/reference/local/

# Python bytecode from the app-icon pipeline (app/scripts/lib/). Generated on every
# run; never an artefact.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.worktrees/

# Agent coordination scratch. These are per-run ack files written into a
# teammate worktree and read from the filesystem, never from git — nothing
# reads them through git ls-files or git show. They carry agent names, session
# ids and absolute home paths, and this repository is the v1 open-source
# launch target, so they do not belong in version control. femcboost has
# carried the same allowlist shape since it adopted the engine.
/.claude/*
